{"_v":1,"id":"les-miserables-1987","bd":{"positive":8,"mixed":0,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Marilyn Stasio","o":"Variety","s":87,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/1987/legit/reviews/les-miserables-9-1200427340/","d":"2014-03-23","q":"As the most exciting musical drama to hit Broadway in some years, as a visually and musically stirring spectacle, as a stellar instance of highly refined staging skill, 'Les Miserables' will be the hit it deserves to be."},{"cn":"Mark Kennedy","o":"Associated Press","s":85,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"http://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2014/mar/23/review-gloomy-glorious-les-miz-hits-broadway/?page=all","d":"2014-03-23","q":"Les Miserables has rolled into town for its third bite at the Broadway apple, and there’s nothing tiresome about its gloomy, aching heartbeat...The melodies are as grandiose as the story. And here, the voices and look of the show wonderfully match. Bring your flag."},{"cn":"Frank Rich","o":"The New York Times","s":71,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/1987/03/13/theater/theater-les-miserables.html","d":"1987-03-13","q":"The elaborate production does serve the music well, and the music is what must carry this show."},{"cn":"Zachary Stewart","o":"TheaterMania","s":87,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://www.theatermania.com/new-york-city-theater/reviews/03-2014/les-miserables_67960.html","d":"2014-03-23","q":"Even the most cynical of theatergoers will find it difficult not to be carried away by the grandeur and sweeping emotion of the evening."},{"cn":"Tulis McCall","o":"New York Theatre Guide","s":81,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.newyorktheatreguide.com/reviews/lesmiserables14.htm","d":"2014-03-24","q":"The voices are so grand that at times it seemed like a contest with the audience applause meter ready to rock after each number."},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Daily News","s":72,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://www.nydailynews.com/entertainment/music-arts/les-miserables-theater-review-article-1.1729631","d":"2014-03-23","q":"What's really outstanding about Broadway's mixed-bag reboot of Les Miserables comes when the show is at its leanest and most minimal: one man, one voice, one prayer."},{"cn":null,"o":"Broadway Voice","s":81,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"https://bwayvoice.com/les-miserables-2/","d":"2014-05-02","q":"Nearly all recommend that it be seen."},{"cn":"Lauren Yarger","o":"Reflections in the Light","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"http://reflectionsinthelight.blogspot.com/2014/04/broadway-theater-review-les-miserables.html#.VPsJkuFk46s","d":"2014-04-04","q":"Ramin Karimloo stars as Jean Valjean -- and he sounds a lot like Colm Wilkinson, who originated the role, so if you have been listening to the original soundtrack for the last 25 years, you're in for a treat with him."}],"hi":"https://images.ctfassets.net/6pezt69ih962/5Ri2YM9GVBYNUf3LgW20QW/ac0b8a3ca8f0c2dd96aa160239c882e4/1471441964012_LES_P322_ToadyTix_480x720.jpg?w=1920&h=800&fit=fill&f=center&fm=webp&q=90","ta":"1681 Broadway, New York, NY 10019","pd":"1987-02-28","ca":[{"n":"Cindy Benson","r":"Woman Worker"},{"n":"Jane Bodle","r":"Woman Worker"},{"n":"David Bryant","r":"Chain Gang"},{"n":"Leo Burmester","r":"Chain Gang"},{"n":"Jennifer Butt","r":"Madame Thénardier"},{"n":"Jesse Corti","r":"Farmer"},{"n":"Anthony Crivello","r":"Bamatabois"},{"n":"Ann Crumb","r":"Factory Girl"},{"n":"Braden Danner","r":"Gavroche"},{"n":"John Dewar","r":"Chain Gang"},{"n":"Joanna Glushak","r":"Woman Worker"},{"n":"Susan Goodman","r":"Innkeeper's Wife"},{"n":"Randy Graff","r":"Fantine"},{"n":"Paul Harman","r":"Chain Gang"},{"n":"Kelli James","r":"Whore"},{"n":"Gretchen Kingsley-Weihe","r":"Whore"},{"n":"Joseph Kolinski","r":"Chain Gang"},{"n":"Judy Kuhn","r":"Whore"},{"n":"Norman Large","r":"Bishop of Digne"},{"n":"Marcus Lovett","r":"Constable"},{"n":"Michael Maguire","r":"Chain Gang"},{"n":"Terrence Mann","r":"Javert"},{"n":"Kevin Marcum","r":"Chain Gang"},{"n":"Chrissie McDonald","r":"Young Eponine"},{"n":"John Norman","r":"Innkeeper"},{"n":"Frances Ruffelle","r":"Whore"},{"n":"Alex Santoriello","r":"Chain Gang"},{"n":"Marcie Shaw","r":"Woman Worker"},{"n":"Steve Shocket","r":"Constable"},{"n":"Donna Vivino","r":"Young Cosette"},{"n":"Colm Wilkinson","r":"Jean Valjean"}]}